window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b291-b2706d75905b775b.json"]={sha256:"b2706d75905b775bfec212bedfbaa6911f650dae74ce1390057d8e432e2a3c61",value:{"id":"b291","title":"浮動碼頭繫泊系統","titleEn":"Mooring systems for floating docks","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"辨識浮碼頭浮力纜繩幾何與岸上通道的耦合反應。課程從邊界辨識與資料整理走到水理量化、構造介面及驗證紀錄；每一步把計算結果連回可量測的證據。十個不同單元分別處理關鍵機制，不以名義尺寸或單一通過率代替整體工程判斷，並明列合成算例與現地資料的差別。","summaryEn":"Identify coupled buoyancy, mooring geometry and shore-access response of floating docks. The course moves from boundary identification and evidence to hydraulic quantification, structural interfaces and verification records. Ten distinct units connect each calculated quantity to measurable evidence. Nominal geometry or a single pass rate does not establish whole-system performance, and synthetic teaching examples remain separate from field observations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-coasts","subcategoryTitle":"海岸、港灣與水資源韌性","subcategoryTitleEn":"Coasts, ports and water-resource resilience","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-coasts","learningTags":["water","water-coasts","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-port","architectureNodes":[["浮台載重與吃水","Pontoon loading and draft"],["水下流阻尺度","Submerged-current drag scale"],["材料伸長與有效剛度","Material extension and effective stiffness"],["並聯恢復剛度","Parallel restoring stiffness"],["浮力儲備與損艙","Buoyant reserve and compartment loss"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-port","labels":["浮台載重與吃水","水下流阻尺度","材料伸長與有效剛度","並聯恢復剛度","浮力儲備與損艙"],"labelsEn":["Pontoon loading and draft","Submerged-current drag scale","Material extension and effective stiffness","Parallel restoring stiffness","Buoyant reserve and compartment loss"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為原創合成算例，不是地標工程的實測或推薦操作值。教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設海水1025kg/m³、水線面100m²、均勻增重10250kg，ΔT=Δm/(ρA)=0.10m；不含傾斜與波浪。假設增重由10250加10%至11275kg、水線面與密度不變，平均吃水增量由0.10變0.11m；並不保證各角點只增加同樣深度。重新計算前先列固定條件、單位、適用尺度及可能失效的邊界。把模型敏感度與測量誤差分開，不能將單一參數變化直接當成工程風險或壽命比例。比較兩次結果後，記錄還需要哪些獨立證據，並由負責專業人員判斷適用性。","textEn":"This original synthetic example is neither a landmark measurement nor a recommended operating value. Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,constant waterplane100m² and uniformly added10250kg. Mean draft increaseΔT=0.10m, excluding heel and waves. Increasing added mass10% from10250 to11275kg at fixed waterplane and density changes mean draft increment from0.10 to0.11m, without guaranteeing equal immersion changes at every corner. Before recalculating, list fixed conditions, units, applicable scale and boundaries that could fail. Separate model sensitivity from measurement uncertainty: a parameter change does not directly give a proportional change in engineering risk or service life. Compare the results, record independent evidence still needed, and have the responsible specialist determine applicability.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b291-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「浮台載重與吃水」與「迎風面與風作用」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pontoon loading and draft\" and \"Windage and wind action\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b291-v15-01","title":"浮台載重與吃水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pontoon loading and draft: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「浮台載重與吃水」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pontoon loading and draft” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"浮碼頭用排水體積平衡總重量，增加人員或設備會改變平均吃水與乾舷。矩形常水線面只是靜水近似，重量位置還影響傾斜，進水或浮筒形狀變化會改變面積；因此承載評估需把平均下沉、偏載與損壞狀態分開，不能只算總浮力。 假設海水1025kg/m³、水線面100m²、均勻增重10250kg，ΔT=Δm/(ρA)=0.10m；不含傾斜與波浪。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「浮台載重與吃水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A floating dock balances total weight through displaced water. Added people or equipment change mean draft and freeboard. A constant rectangular waterplane is only a calm-water approximation; weight location causes heel, while flooding or changing hull shape alters area. Assessment must separate mean immersion, eccentric loading and damage rather than relying on one total-buoyancy figure for every condition. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,constant waterplane100m² and uniformly added10250kg. Mean draft increaseΔT=0.10m, excluding heel and waves. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pontoon loading and draft” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「浮台載重與吃水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pontoon loading and draft”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-01-k1","title":"浮台載重與吃水","titleEn":"Pontoon loading and draft","text":"浮碼頭用排水體積平衡總重量，增加人員或設備會改變平均吃水與乾舷。矩形常水線面只是靜水近似，重量位置還影響傾斜，進水或浮筒形狀變化會改變面積；因此承載評估需把平均下沉、偏載與損壞狀態分開，不能只算總浮力。","textEn":"A floating dock balances total weight through displaced water. Added people or equipment change mean draft and freeboard.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「浮台載重與吃水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pontoon loading and draft\" is correct?","options":["只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。","浮碼頭用排水體積平衡總重量，增加人員或設備會改變平均吃水與乾舷。","浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。"],"optionsEn":["Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves.","A floating dock balances total weight through displaced water.","Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels."],"answer":1,"explanation":"浮碼頭用排水體積平衡總重量，增加人員或設備會改變平均吃水與乾舷。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A floating dock balances total weight through displaced water. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b291-v15-02","title":"浮台載重與吃水：定量估算","titleEn":"Pontoon loading and draft: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「浮台載重與吃水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pontoon loading and draft” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設海水1025kg/m³、水線面100m²、均勻增重10250kg，ΔT=Δm/(ρA)=0.10m；不含傾斜與波浪。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,constant waterplane100m² and uniformly added10250kg. Mean draft increaseΔT=0.10m, excluding heel and waves. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用多角點吃水與重量清單交叉核對，標出人員和設備可能集中區，檢查水線面是否隨吃水改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare corner drafts with the weight schedule, marking potential concentrated occupancy and checking whether waterplane changes with immersion.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設海水1025kg/m³、水線面100m²、均勻增重10250kg，ΔT=Δm/(ρA)=0.10m；不含傾斜與波浪。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,constant waterplane100m² and uniformly added10250kg. Mean draft increaseΔT=0.10m, excluding heel and waves.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「浮台載重與吃水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pontoon loading and draft\", which statement holds?","options":["纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。","浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry.","If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b291-v15-03","title":"浮台載重與吃水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pontoon loading and draft: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「浮台載重與吃水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pontoon loading and draft” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用多角點吃水與重量清單交叉核對，標出人員和設備可能集中區，檢查水線面是否隨吃水改變。另記密閉艙狀態及最低乾舷，把靜水預算與實際使用限制分開保存。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare corner drafts with the weight schedule, marking potential concentrated occupancy and checking whether waterplane changes with immersion. Record compartment condition and minimum freeboard, keeping this static budget distinct from the actual restrictions governing use of the facility. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用多角點吃水與重量清單交叉核對，標出人員和設備可能集中區，檢查水線面是否隨吃水改變。另記密閉艙狀態及最低乾舷，把靜水預算與實際使用限制分開保存。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare corner drafts with the weight schedule, marking potential concentrated occupancy and checking whether waterplane changes with immersion. Record compartment condition and minimum freeboard, keeping this static budget distinct from the actual restrictions governing use of the facility.","failure":"注意干擾：偏載時平均吃水正常仍可能有一角進水，未察覺艙漏又使有效浮力持續減少。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Eccentric loading can flood a corner despite normal mean draft, and unnoticed leakage progressively reduces buoyant reserve. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用多角點吃水與重量清單交叉核對，標出人員和設備可能集中區，檢查水線面是否隨吃水改變。另記密閉艙狀態及最低乾舷，把靜水預算與實際使用限制分開保存。","textEn":"Compare corner drafts with the weight schedule, marking potential concentrated occupancy and checking whether waterplane changes with immersion. Record compartment condition and minimum freeboard, keeping this static budget distinct from the actual restrictions governing use of the facility.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用多角點吃水與重量清單交叉核對，標出人員和設備可能集中區，檢查水線面是否隨吃水改變。另記密閉艙狀態及最低乾舷，把靜水預算與實際使用限制分開保存。","textEn":"Compare corner drafts with the weight schedule, marking potential concentrated occupancy and checking whether waterplane changes with immersion. Record compartment condition and minimum freeboard, keeping this static budget distinct from the actual restrictions governing use of the facility.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「浮台載重與吃水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pontoon loading and draft\"?","options":["用多角點吃水與重量清單交叉核對，標出人員和設備可能集中區，檢查水線面是否隨吃水改變。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。"],"optionsEn":["Compare corner drafts with the weight schedule, marking potential concentrated occupancy and checking whether waterplane changes with immersion.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用多角點吃水與重量清單交叉核對，標出人員和設備可能集中區，檢查水線面是否隨吃水改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare corner drafts with the weight schedule, marking potential concentrated occupancy and checking whether waterplane changes with immersion. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b291-v15-04","title":"浮台載重與吃水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pontoon loading and draft: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「浮台載重與吃水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pontoon loading and draft” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"偏載時平均吃水正常仍可能有一角進水，未察覺艙漏又使有效浮力持續減少。只核對設計總重量，無法辨識局部低乾舷與失去密閉性的共同影響。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Eccentric loading can flood a corner despite normal mean draft, and unnoticed leakage progressively reduces buoyant reserve. Checking design total weight alone cannot reveal the combined effect of local low freeboard and compromised compartment integrity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設海水1025kg/m³、水線面100m²、均勻增重10250kg，ΔT=Δm/(ρA)=0.10m；不含傾斜與波浪。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mean draft increaseΔT=0.10m, excluding heel and waves.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"偏載時平均吃水正常仍可能有一角進水，未察覺艙漏又使有效浮力持續減少。只核對設計總重量，無法辨識局部低乾舷與失去密閉性的共同影響。","textEn":"Eccentric loading can flood a corner despite normal mean draft, and unnoticed leakage progressively reduces buoyant reserve. Checking design total weight alone cannot reveal the combined effect of local low freeboard and compromised compartment integrity.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「浮台載重與吃水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pontoon loading and draft\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","偏載時平均吃水正常仍可能有一角進水，未察覺艙漏又使有效浮力持續減少。","浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Eccentric loading can flood a corner despite normal mean draft, and unnoticed leakage progressively reduces buoyant reserve.","Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels."],"answer":1,"explanation":"偏載時平均吃水正常仍可能有一角進水，未察覺艙漏又使有效浮力持續減少。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Eccentric loading can flood a corner despite normal mean draft, and unnoticed leakage progressively reduces buoyant reserve. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b291-v15-05","title":"迎風面與風作用：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Windage and wind action: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「迎風面與風作用」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Windage and wind action” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"浮碼頭與繫泊船舶的迎風面共同傳力，風向改變會讓受力位置與扭矩不同。平方風速式使用指定平均時間與高度，不能把瞬間陣風和長期平均混在同一係數下；遮蔽、上層設施及船舶配置也會改變受風面，需追蹤實際組合。 假設空氣ρ=1.225kg/m³、Cd=1.2、投影面積100m²、指定風速20m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN；非操作門檻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「迎風面與風作用」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The dock and attached vessels contribute windage and transfer load together; direction changes force location and torque. A quadratic wind relation requires a specified averaging period and elevation, rather than mixing gusts and long-term means under one coefficient. Shelter, superstructures and vessel arrangements also change projected area, making the actual combined configuration part of the load case. Assume air1.225kg/m³,Cd=1.2,projected area100m² and selected speed20m/s. F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN, not an operating threshold. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Windage and wind action” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「迎風面與風作用」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Windage and wind action”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-05-k1","title":"迎風面與風作用","titleEn":"Windage and wind action","text":"浮碼頭與繫泊船舶的迎風面共同傳力，風向改變會讓受力位置與扭矩不同。平方風速式使用指定平均時間與高度，不能把瞬間陣風和長期平均混在同一係數下；遮蔽、上層設施及船舶配置也會改變受風面，需追蹤實際組合。","textEn":"The dock and attached vessels contribute windage and transfer load together; direction changes force location and torque. A quadratic wind relation requires a specified averaging period and elevation, rather than mixing gusts and long-term means under one coefficient.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「迎風面與風作用」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Windage and wind action\" is correct?","options":["浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。","遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。","浮碼頭與繫泊船舶的迎風面共同傳力，風向改變會讓受力位置與扭矩不同。"],"optionsEn":["Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels.","A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface.","The dock and attached vessels contribute windage and transfer load together; direction changes force location and torque."],"answer":2,"explanation":"浮碼頭與繫泊船舶的迎風面共同傳力，風向改變會讓受力位置與扭矩不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The dock and attached vessels contribute windage and transfer load together; direction changes force location and torque. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b291-v15-06","title":"迎風面與風作用：定量估算","titleEn":"Windage and wind action: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「迎風面與風作用」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Windage and wind action” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設空氣ρ=1.225kg/m³、Cd=1.2、投影面積100m²、指定風速20m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN；非操作門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume air1.225kg/m³,Cd=1.2,projected area100m² and selected speed20m/s. F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN, not an operating threshold. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在平面與立面標出迎風投影、合力高度及係纜點，核對風速定義與量測位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map projected area, force height and mooring points and check wind-speed definition and measurement location.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設空氣ρ=1.225kg/m³、Cd=1.2、投影面積100m²、指定風速20m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN；非操作門檻。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume air1.225kg/m³,Cd=1.2,projected area100m² and selected speed20m/s. F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN, not an operating threshold.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「迎風面與風作用」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Windage and wind action\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。","所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling.","Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b291-v15-07","title":"迎風面與風作用：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Windage and wind action: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「迎風面與風作用」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Windage and wind action” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在平面與立面標出迎風投影、合力高度及係纜點，核對風速定義與量測位置。比較不同船舶和風向配置，將遮蔽證據與未遮蔽情境分開，保留由偏心造成的扭矩需求。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map projected area, force height and mooring points and check wind-speed definition and measurement location. Compare vessel and directional configurations, separating evidenced shelter from exposed conditions and retaining torque demand created by an eccentric line of action. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在平面與立面標出迎風投影、合力高度及係纜點，核對風速定義與量測位置。比較不同船舶和風向配置，將遮蔽證據與未遮蔽情境分開，保留由偏心造成的扭矩需求。","observationEn":"Site practice: Map projected area, force height and mooring points and check wind-speed definition and measurement location. Compare vessel and directional configurations, separating evidenced shelter from exposed conditions and retaining torque demand created by an eccentric line of action.","failure":"注意干擾：新增遮棚或高船舶可增加迎風面及力矩，沿用空碼頭參數會低估系統需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A canopy or taller vessel increases windage and torque, so empty-dock parameters understate demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在平面與立面標出迎風投影、合力高度及係纜點，核對風速定義與量測位置。比較不同船舶和風向配置，將遮蔽證據與未遮蔽情境分開，保留由偏心造成的扭矩需求。","textEn":"Map projected area, force height and mooring points and check wind-speed definition and measurement location. Compare vessel and directional configurations, separating evidenced shelter from exposed conditions and retaining torque demand created by an eccentric line of action.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在平面與立面標出迎風投影、合力高度及係纜點，核對風速定義與量測位置。比較不同船舶和風向配置，將遮蔽證據與未遮蔽情境分開，保留由偏心造成的扭矩需求。","textEn":"Map projected area, force height and mooring points and check wind-speed definition and measurement location. Compare vessel and directional configurations, separating evidenced shelter from exposed conditions and retaining torque demand created by an eccentric line of action.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「迎風面與風作用」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Windage and wind action\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在平面與立面標出迎風投影、合力高度及係纜點，核對風速定義與量測位置。","引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Map projected area, force height and mooring points and check wind-speed definition and measurement location.","Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在平面與立面標出迎風投影、合力高度及係纜點，核對風速定義與量測位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map projected area, force height and mooring points and check wind-speed definition and measurement location. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b291-v15-08","title":"迎風面與風作用：失效診斷","titleEn":"Windage and wind action: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「迎風面與風作用」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Windage and wind action” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"新增遮棚或高船舶可增加迎風面及力矩，沿用空碼頭參數會低估系統需求。平均風速與陣風混用則可能把不同時間尺度的作用錯誤相加或相互抵銷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A canopy or taller vessel increases windage and torque, so empty-dock parameters understate demand. Mixing mean wind and gust definitions can also incorrectly combine or cancel actions occurring on different response timescales in the system. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設空氣ρ=1.225kg/m³、Cd=1.2、投影面積100m²、指定風速20m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN；非操作門檻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN, not an operating threshold.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"新增遮棚或高船舶可增加迎風面及力矩，沿用空碼頭參數會低估系統需求。平均風速與陣風混用則可能把不同時間尺度的作用錯誤相加或相互抵銷。","textEn":"A canopy or taller vessel increases windage and torque, so empty-dock parameters understate demand. Mixing mean wind and gust definitions can also incorrectly combine or cancel actions occurring on different response timescales in the system.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「迎風面與風作用」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Windage and wind action\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。","新增遮棚或高船舶可增加迎風面及力矩，沿用空碼頭參數會低估系統需求。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface.","A canopy or taller vessel increases windage and torque, so empty-dock parameters understate demand."],"answer":2,"explanation":"新增遮棚或高船舶可增加迎風面及力矩，沿用空碼頭參數會低估系統需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A canopy or taller vessel increases windage and torque, so empty-dock parameters understate demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b291-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「水下流阻尺度」與「纜繩力向分解」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Submerged-current drag scale\" and \"Resolving mooring-line forces\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b291-v15-09","title":"水下流阻尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Submerged-current drag scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「水下流阻尺度」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Submerged-current drag scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水流作用在浮體水下投影及附掛設備，水位與吃水改變會更新受流面。均勻穩定流估算沒有涵蓋波浪加速度或渦激反應，狹窄通道與船間流場又會加速；分析應將力向、作用點及變動時間列明，避免把平均流速當成完整動態作用。 假設海水1025kg/m³、Cd=1.0、水下面積20m²、均勻流1.5m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=23.0625kN；不含波浪慣性。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水下流阻尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Current acts on the submerged projection and attached equipment, which change with draft and water level. A uniform steady estimate excludes wave acceleration and vortex response, while narrow passages or vessel gaps can accelerate flow. Direction, force location and timescale therefore need explicit treatment; mean current speed does not by itself describe the complete dynamic action on the moored assembly. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,Cd=1.0,submerged area20m² and uniform current1.5m/s. Steady drag is23.0625kN, excluding wave inertia. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Submerged-current drag scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水下流阻尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Submerged-current drag scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-09-k1","title":"水下流阻尺度","titleEn":"Submerged-current drag scale","text":"水流作用在浮體水下投影及附掛設備，水位與吃水改變會更新受流面。均勻穩定流估算沒有涵蓋波浪加速度或渦激反應，狹窄通道與船間流場又會加速；分析應將力向、作用點及變動時間列明，避免把平均流速當成完整動態作用。","textEn":"Current acts on the submerged projection and attached equipment, which change with draft and water level. A uniform steady estimate excludes wave acceleration and vortex response, while narrow passages or vessel gaps can accelerate flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水下流阻尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Submerged-current drag scale\" is correct?","options":["水流作用在浮體水下投影及附掛設備，水位與吃水改變會更新受流面。","遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。","纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。"],"optionsEn":["Current acts on the submerged projection and attached equipment, which change with draft and water level.","A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface.","Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水流作用在浮體水下投影及附掛設備，水位與吃水改變會更新受流面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Current acts on the submerged projection and attached equipment, which change with draft and water level. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b291-v15-10","title":"水下流阻尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Submerged-current drag scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水下流阻尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Submerged-current drag scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設海水1025kg/m³、Cd=1.0、水下面積20m²、均勻流1.5m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=23.0625kN；不含波浪慣性。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,Cd=1.0,submerged area20m² and uniform current1.5m/s. Steady drag is23.0625kN, excluding wave inertia. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測不同深度與流向的速度並記錄吃水，核對水下突起和海生物附著是否納入投影。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure speed by depth and direction with draft, checking projections of appendages and marine growth.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設海水1025kg/m³、Cd=1.0、水下面積20m²、均勻流1.5m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=23.0625kN；不含波浪慣性。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,Cd=1.0,submerged area20m² and uniform current1.5m/s. Steady drag is23.0625kN, excluding wave inertia.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水下流阻尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Submerged-current drag scale\", which statement holds?","options":["浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。"],"optionsEn":["If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b291-v15-11","title":"水下流阻尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Submerged-current drag scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水下流阻尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Submerged-current drag scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測不同深度與流向的速度並記錄吃水，核對水下突起和海生物附著是否納入投影。將波浪與潮流資料同步，分開穩定拖曳和動態分量，避免用單點緩流區代表整個浮體。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure speed by depth and direction with draft, checking projections of appendages and marine growth. Synchronize wave and tide records and distinguish steady drag from dynamic components rather than representing the full submerged body with one sheltered measurement point. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：量測不同深度與流向的速度並記錄吃水，核對水下突起和海生物附著是否納入投影。將波浪與潮流資料同步，分開穩定拖曳和動態分量，避免用單點緩流區代表整個浮體。","observationEn":"Site practice: Measure speed by depth and direction with draft, checking projections of appendages and marine growth. Synchronize wave and tide records and distinguish steady drag from dynamic components rather than representing the full submerged body with one sheltered measurement point.","failure":"注意干擾：潮向反轉會讓不同纜繩承力，漏掉水下附掛物則低估面積。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Tidal reversal engages different lines, and omitted submerged attachments understate area. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測不同深度與流向的速度並記錄吃水，核對水下突起和海生物附著是否納入投影。將波浪與潮流資料同步，分開穩定拖曳和動態分量，避免用單點緩流區代表整個浮體。","textEn":"Measure speed by depth and direction with draft, checking projections of appendages and marine growth. Synchronize wave and tide records and distinguish steady drag from dynamic components rather than representing the full submerged body with one sheltered measurement point.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"量測不同深度與流向的速度並記錄吃水，核對水下突起和海生物附著是否納入投影。將波浪與潮流資料同步，分開穩定拖曳和動態分量，避免用單點緩流區代表整個浮體。","textEn":"Measure speed by depth and direction with draft, checking projections of appendages and marine growth. Synchronize wave and tide records and distinguish steady drag from dynamic components rather than representing the full submerged body with one sheltered measurement point.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水下流阻尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Submerged-current drag scale\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。","量測不同深度與流向的速度並記錄吃水，核對水下突起和海生物附著是否納入投影。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading.","Measure speed by depth and direction with draft, checking projections of appendages and marine growth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測不同深度與流向的速度並記錄吃水，核對水下突起和海生物附著是否納入投影。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure speed by depth and direction with draft, checking projections of appendages and marine growth. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b291-v15-12","title":"水下流阻尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Submerged-current drag scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水下流阻尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Submerged-current drag scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"潮向反轉會讓不同纜繩承力，漏掉水下附掛物則低估面積。若水流被船體間隙加速，遠處量到的背景速度可能無法代表真正控制局部連接的流場。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Tidal reversal engages different lines, and omitted submerged attachments understate area. Flow accelerated through vessel gaps means distant background measurements may not represent the conditions controlling a particular connection or part of the floating structure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設海水1025kg/m³、Cd=1.0、水下面積20m²、均勻流1.5m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=23.0625kN；不含波浪慣性。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Steady drag is23.0625kN, excluding wave inertia.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"潮向反轉會讓不同纜繩承力，漏掉水下附掛物則低估面積。若水流被船體間隙加速，遠處量到的背景速度可能無法代表真正控制局部連接的流場。","textEn":"Tidal reversal engages different lines, and omitted submerged attachments understate area. Flow accelerated through vessel gaps means distant background measurements may not represent the conditions controlling a particular connection or part of the floating structure.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水下流阻尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Submerged-current drag scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["潮向反轉會讓不同纜繩承力，漏掉水下附掛物則低估面積。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。"],"optionsEn":["Tidal reversal engages different lines, and omitted submerged attachments understate area.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"潮向反轉會讓不同纜繩承力，漏掉水下附掛物則低估面積。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Tidal reversal engages different lines, and omitted submerged attachments understate area. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b291-v15-13","title":"纜繩力向分解：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Resolving mooring-line forces: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「纜繩力向分解」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Resolving mooring-line forces” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"係纜的軸向張力只有投影分量抵抗指定水平力，平面角與垂直角均會影響傳力。理想兩索對稱必須同時張緊才可平均分擔，預張力、鬆弛與彈性差異會破壞此條件；不能將幾何張力直接當成纜具額定能力或現場張緊設定。 假設水平力40kN由兩條水平對稱張緊纜承受，各與力向30°，T=40/(2cos30°)=23.094kN；未含預張與動載。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「纜繩力向分解」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Only a line's projected tension resists the selected horizontal action, with both plan and vertical angles affecting transfer. Two symmetric lines share equally only when simultaneously engaged. Pretension, slack and different elasticity invalidate this assumption, so geometric tension is not the rated capacity of the hardware or an instruction for setting line tension during actual mooring operations. Assume horizontal40kN resisted by two taut horizontal symmetric lines30°from the force direction. T=23.094kN each, excluding pretension and dynamics. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Resolving mooring-line forces” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「纜繩力向分解」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Resolving mooring-line forces”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-13-k1","title":"纜繩力向分解","titleEn":"Resolving mooring-line forces","text":"係纜的軸向張力只有投影分量抵抗指定水平力，平面角與垂直角均會影響傳力。理想兩索對稱必須同時張緊才可平均分擔，預張力、鬆弛與彈性差異會破壞此條件；不能將幾何張力直接當成纜具額定能力或現場張緊設定。","textEn":"Only a line's projected tension resists the selected horizontal action, with both plan and vertical angles affecting transfer. Two symmetric lines share equally only when simultaneously engaged.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「纜繩力向分解」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Resolving mooring-line forces\" is correct?","options":["纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。","係纜的軸向張力只有投影分量抵抗指定水平力，平面角與垂直角均會影響傳力。","所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry.","Only a line's projected tension resists the selected horizontal action, with both plan and vertical angles affecting transfer.","Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"係纜的軸向張力只有投影分量抵抗指定水平力，平面角與垂直角均會影響傳力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Only a line's projected tension resists the selected horizontal action, with both plan and vertical angles affecting transfer. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b291-v15-14","title":"纜繩力向分解：定量估算","titleEn":"Resolving mooring-line forces: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「纜繩力向分解」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Resolving mooring-line forces” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水平力40kN由兩條水平對稱張緊纜承受，各與力向30°，T=40/(2cos30°)=23.094kN；未含預張與動載。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume horizontal40kN resisted by two taut horizontal symmetric lines30°from the force direction. T=23.094kN each, excluding pretension and dynamics. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：畫每條纜的三維方向和自由體圖，確認角度參考軸及同時受力條件，分開預張與荷載增量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw each line in three dimensions and define angle reference and simultaneous engagement, separating pretension from load increment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水平力40kN由兩條水平對稱張緊纜承受，各與力向30°，T=40/(2cos30°)=23.094kN；未含預張與動載。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume horizontal40kN resisted by two taut horizontal symmetric lines30°from the force direction. T=23.094kN each, excluding pretension and dynamics.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「纜繩力向分解」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Resolving mooring-line forces\", which statement holds?","options":["所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。","引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction.","Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b291-v15-15","title":"纜繩力向分解：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Resolving mooring-line forces: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「纜繩力向分解」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Resolving mooring-line forces” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"畫每條纜的三維方向和自由體圖，確認角度參考軸及同時受力條件，分開預張與荷載增量。沿纜具、連接和岸上錨點追蹤力路徑，核對不均分時的替代情境。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw each line in three dimensions and define angle reference and simultaneous engagement, separating pretension from load increment. Trace force through rope, fittings and shore anchorage and evaluate alternative sharing when the symmetric assumption is not supported. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫每條纜的三維方向和自由體圖，確認角度參考軸及同時受力條件，分開預張與荷載增量。沿纜具、連接和岸上錨點追蹤力路徑，核對不均分時的替代情境。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw each line in three dimensions and define angle reference and simultaneous engagement, separating pretension from load increment. Trace force through rope, fittings and shore anchorage and evaluate alternative sharing when the symmetric assumption is not supported.","failure":"注意干擾：一條纜鬆弛時另一條可能承擔大部分需求，垂直角增加又減少水平分量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One slack line shifts much of the demand to another, and vertical inclination reduces horizontal resistance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫每條纜的三維方向和自由體圖，確認角度參考軸及同時受力條件，分開預張與荷載增量。沿纜具、連接和岸上錨點追蹤力路徑，核對不均分時的替代情境。","textEn":"Draw each line in three dimensions and define angle reference and simultaneous engagement, separating pretension from load increment. Trace force through rope, fittings and shore anchorage and evaluate alternative sharing when the symmetric assumption is not supported.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫每條纜的三維方向和自由體圖，確認角度參考軸及同時受力條件，分開預張與荷載增量。沿纜具、連接和岸上錨點追蹤力路徑，核對不均分時的替代情境。","textEn":"Draw each line in three dimensions and define angle reference and simultaneous engagement, separating pretension from load increment. Trace force through rope, fittings and shore anchorage and evaluate alternative sharing when the symmetric assumption is not supported.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「纜繩力向分解」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Resolving mooring-line forces\"?","options":["畫每條纜的三維方向和自由體圖，確認角度參考軸及同時受力條件，分開預張與荷載增量。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。"],"optionsEn":["Draw each line in three dimensions and define angle reference and simultaneous engagement, separating pretension from load increment.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves."],"answer":0,"explanation":"畫每條纜的三維方向和自由體圖，確認角度參考軸及同時受力條件，分開預張與荷載增量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw each line in three dimensions and define angle reference and simultaneous engagement, separating pretension from load increment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b291-v15-16","title":"纜繩力向分解：失效診斷","titleEn":"Resolving mooring-line forces: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「纜繩力向分解」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Resolving mooring-line forces” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"一條纜鬆弛時另一條可能承擔大部分需求，垂直角增加又減少水平分量。僅靠纜數平均分配，會漏掉不對稱姿態及突然繃緊造成的衝擊。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One slack line shifts much of the demand to another, and vertical inclination reduces horizontal resistance. Dividing load only by line count misses asymmetric geometry and impact when a previously slack line suddenly becomes taut. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設水平力40kN由兩條水平對稱張緊纜承受，各與力向30°，T=40/(2cos30°)=23.094kN；未含預張與動載。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: T=23.094kN each, excluding pretension and dynamics.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"一條纜鬆弛時另一條可能承擔大部分需求，垂直角增加又減少水平分量。僅靠纜數平均分配，會漏掉不對稱姿態及突然繃緊造成的衝擊。","textEn":"One slack line shifts much of the demand to another, and vertical inclination reduces horizontal resistance. Dividing load only by line count misses asymmetric geometry and impact when a previously slack line suddenly becomes taut.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「纜繩力向分解」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Resolving mooring-line forces\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","一條纜鬆弛時另一條可能承擔大部分需求，垂直角增加又減少水平分量。","所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","One slack line shifts much of the demand to another, and vertical inclination reduces horizontal resistance.","Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"一條纜鬆弛時另一條可能承擔大部分需求，垂直角增加又減少水平分量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One slack line shifts much of the demand to another, and vertical inclination reduces horizontal resistance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b291-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「材料伸長與有效剛度」與「潮位幾何與鬆弛」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Material extension and effective stiffness\" and \"Tidal geometry and slack\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b291-v15-17","title":"材料伸長與有效剛度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Material extension and effective stiffness: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「材料伸長與有效剛度」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Material extension and effective stiffness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"纜繩伸長包含材料應變與編織重排，許多材料在循環中有遲滯、徐變和不同切線剛度。直桿彈性式只是一個局部基準，不適合把所有纜索都當鋼杆；量測時還需分開初始鬆弛與幾何拉直，否則剛度估計會隨量測區間改變。 假設直線彈性纜有效EA=5000kN、長20m、張力增量25kN，伸長ΔL=ΔTL/(EA)=0.10m；不含鬆弛與徐變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「材料伸長與有效剛度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Line extension combines material strain with constructional rearrangement, and many ropes show hysteresis, creep and changing tangent stiffness. A straight elastic rod is a local baseline rather than a universal steel-like representation. Initial slack and geometric straightening must be separated from material extension, otherwise the inferred stiffness depends on which portion of the load-displacement path was measured. Assume a straight elastic line with effective EA=5000kN,length20m and tension increment25kN. Extension is0.10m, excluding slack and creep. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Material extension and effective stiffness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「材料伸長與有效剛度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Material extension and effective stiffness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-17-k1","title":"材料伸長與有效剛度","titleEn":"Material extension and effective stiffness","text":"纜繩伸長包含材料應變與編織重排，許多材料在循環中有遲滯、徐變和不同切線剛度。直桿彈性式只是一個局部基準，不適合把所有纜索都當鋼杆；量測時還需分開初始鬆弛與幾何拉直，否則剛度估計會隨量測區間改變。","textEn":"Line extension combines material strain with constructional rearrangement, and many ropes show hysteresis, creep and changing tangent stiffness. A straight elastic rod is a local baseline rather than a universal steel-like representation.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「材料伸長與有效剛度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Material extension and effective stiffness\" is correct?","options":["所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。","浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。","纜繩伸長包含材料應變與編織重排，許多材料在循環中有遲滯、徐變和不同切線剛度。"],"optionsEn":["Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling.","If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.","Line extension combines material strain with constructional rearrangement, and many ropes show hysteresis, creep and changing tangent stiffness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"纜繩伸長包含材料應變與編織重排，許多材料在循環中有遲滯、徐變和不同切線剛度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Line extension combines material strain with constructional rearrangement, and many ropes show hysteresis, creep and changing tangent stiffness. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b291-v15-18","title":"材料伸長與有效剛度：定量估算","titleEn":"Material extension and effective stiffness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「材料伸長與有效剛度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Material extension and effective stiffness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設直線彈性纜有效EA=5000kN、長20m、張力增量25kN，伸長ΔL=ΔTL/(EA)=0.10m；不含鬆弛與徐變。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a straight elastic line with effective EA=5000kN,length20m and tension increment25kN. Extension is0.10m, excluding slack and creep. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：使用相符含水與循環條件的試驗曲線，明列有效標距並分離預張階段。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use response curves under relevant moisture and cycling, defining gauge length and separating pretension.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設直線彈性纜有效EA=5000kN、長20m、張力增量25kN，伸長ΔL=ΔTL/(EA)=0.10m；不含鬆弛與徐變。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a straight elastic line with effective EA=5000kN,length20m and tension increment25kN. Extension is0.10m, excluding slack and creep.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「材料伸長與有效剛度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Material extension and effective stiffness\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。","理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information.","All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b291-v15-19","title":"材料伸長與有效剛度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Material extension and effective stiffness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「材料伸長與有效剛度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Material extension and effective stiffness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"使用相符含水與循環條件的試驗曲線，明列有效標距並分離預張階段。比較載入卸載與長時間保持資料，確認計算用割線或切線剛度，避免以單次拉伸斜率代表全部壽期。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use response curves under relevant moisture and cycling, defining gauge length and separating pretension. Compare loading, unloading and hold periods, identify secant versus tangent stiffness, and avoid representing the entire service history by one slope from a single tensile test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：使用相符含水與循環條件的試驗曲線，明列有效標距並分離預張階段。比較載入卸載與長時間保持資料，確認計算用割線或切線剛度，避免以單次拉伸斜率代表全部壽期。","observationEn":"Site practice: Use response curves under relevant moisture and cycling, defining gauge length and separating pretension. Compare loading, unloading and hold periods, identify secant versus tangent stiffness, and avoid representing the entire service history by one slope from a single tensile test.","failure":"注意干擾：將編織收緊當材料彈性會低估後續切線剛度，長時間徐變又可能增加鬆弛和位移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mistaking constructional tightening for elasticity understates later tangent stiffness, while creep adds slack and displacement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"使用相符含水與循環條件的試驗曲線，明列有效標距並分離預張階段。比較載入卸載與長時間保持資料，確認計算用割線或切線剛度，避免以單次拉伸斜率代表全部壽期。","textEn":"Use response curves under relevant moisture and cycling, defining gauge length and separating pretension. Compare loading, unloading and hold periods, identify secant versus tangent stiffness, and avoid representing the entire service history by one slope from a single tensile test.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"使用相符含水與循環條件的試驗曲線，明列有效標距並分離預張階段。比較載入卸載與長時間保持資料，確認計算用割線或切線剛度，避免以單次拉伸斜率代表全部壽期。","textEn":"Use response curves under relevant moisture and cycling, defining gauge length and separating pretension. Compare loading, unloading and hold periods, identify secant versus tangent stiffness, and avoid representing the entire service history by one slope from a single tensile test.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「材料伸長與有效剛度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Material extension and effective stiffness\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","使用相符含水與循環條件的試驗曲線，明列有效標距並分離預張階段。","浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use response curves under relevant moisture and cycling, defining gauge length and separating pretension.","Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels."],"answer":1,"explanation":"使用相符含水與循環條件的試驗曲線，明列有效標距並分離預張階段。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use response curves under relevant moisture and cycling, defining gauge length and separating pretension. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b291-v15-20","title":"材料伸長與有效剛度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Material extension and effective stiffness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「材料伸長與有效剛度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Material extension and effective stiffness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將編織收緊當材料彈性會低估後續切線剛度，長時間徐變又可能增加鬆弛和位移。相同最終伸長下，張力歷史與儲能可以不同，不能只讀總長度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mistaking constructional tightening for elasticity understates later tangent stiffness, while creep adds slack and displacement. Equal final extension can conceal different tension histories and stored energy, so total line length alone is insufficient for interpreting response. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設直線彈性纜有效EA=5000kN、長20m、張力增量25kN，伸長ΔL=ΔTL/(EA)=0.10m；不含鬆弛與徐變。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Extension is0.10m, excluding slack and creep.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將編織收緊當材料彈性會低估後續切線剛度，長時間徐變又可能增加鬆弛和位移。相同最終伸長下，張力歷史與儲能可以不同，不能只讀總長度。","textEn":"Mistaking constructional tightening for elasticity understates later tangent stiffness, while creep adds slack and displacement. Equal final extension can conceal different tension histories and stored energy, so total line length alone is insufficient for interpreting response.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「材料伸長與有效剛度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Material extension and effective stiffness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。","將編織收緊當材料彈性會低估後續切線剛度，長時間徐變又可能增加鬆弛和位移。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.","Mistaking constructional tightening for elasticity understates later tangent stiffness, while creep adds slack and displacement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將編織收緊當材料彈性會低估後續切線剛度，長時間徐變又可能增加鬆弛和位移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mistaking constructional tightening for elasticity understates later tangent stiffness, while creep adds slack and displacement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b291-v15-21","title":"潮位幾何與鬆弛：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tidal geometry and slack: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「潮位幾何與鬆弛」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tidal geometry and slack” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"岸上固定點與浮台的高差隨潮位變化，連線長度及入射角因此改變，即使平面位置未動也可能拉緊纜繩。直線距離只是幾何下限，鏈條垂度和海床接觸另影響反力；不能把一段預留長度視為在所有水位都具有相同的鬆弛餘量。 假設水平距10m，高差由1變3m，直線距由√101=10.0499增至√109=10.4403m，增0.3904m；非鏈條張力模型。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「潮位幾何與鬆弛」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The height difference between a shore point and a pontoon varies with tide, changing chord length and angle even without horizontal motion. Straight-line distance is a geometric lower bound; chain sag and bed contact separately affect reaction. A reserved length therefore does not provide the same slack margin at every water level or imply unchanged horizontal restoring behavior. Assume horizontal distance10m and height difference1to3m. Chord length rises10.0499to10.4403m, an increase0.3904m; this is not a catenary-tension model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tidal geometry and slack” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「潮位幾何與鬆弛」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tidal geometry and slack”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-21-k1","title":"潮位幾何與鬆弛","titleEn":"Tidal geometry and slack","text":"岸上固定點與浮台的高差隨潮位變化，連線長度及入射角因此改變，即使平面位置未動也可能拉緊纜繩。直線距離只是幾何下限，鏈條垂度和海床接觸另影響反力；不能把一段預留長度視為在所有水位都具有相同的鬆弛餘量。","textEn":"The height difference between a shore point and a pontoon varies with tide, changing chord length and angle even without horizontal motion. Straight-line distance is a geometric lower bound; chain sag and bed contact separately affect reaction.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「潮位幾何與鬆弛」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tidal geometry and slack\" is correct?","options":["岸上固定點與浮台的高差隨潮位變化，連線長度及入射角因此改變，即使平面位置未動也可能拉緊纜繩。","浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。","所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。"],"optionsEn":["The height difference between a shore point and a pontoon varies with tide, changing chord length and angle even without horizontal motion.","If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.","Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"岸上固定點與浮台的高差隨潮位變化，連線長度及入射角因此改變，即使平面位置未動也可能拉緊纜繩。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The height difference between a shore point and a pontoon varies with tide, changing chord length and angle even without horizontal motion. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b291-v15-22","title":"潮位幾何與鬆弛：定量估算","titleEn":"Tidal geometry and slack: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「潮位幾何與鬆弛」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tidal geometry and slack” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水平距10m，高差由1變3m，直線距由√101=10.0499增至√109=10.4403m，增0.3904m；非鏈條張力模型。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume horizontal distance10m and height difference1to3m. Chord length rises10.0499to10.4403m, an increase0.3904m; this is not a catenary-tension model. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同一基準畫高低水位的纜端位置，量測可用纜長、垂度和海床接觸，核對可能卡阻。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot line-end positions at different levels on one datum, measuring available length, sag and seabed contact and checking obstructions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水平距10m，高差由1變3m，直線距由√101=10.0499增至√109=10.4403m，增0.3904m；非鏈條張力模型。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume horizontal distance10m and height difference1to3m. Chord length rises10.0499to10.4403m, an increase0.3904m; this is not a catenary-tension model.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「潮位幾何與鬆弛」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tidal geometry and slack\", which statement holds?","options":["引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。"],"optionsEn":["Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b291-v15-23","title":"潮位幾何與鬆弛：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tidal geometry and slack: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「潮位幾何與鬆弛」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tidal geometry and slack” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同一基準畫高低水位的纜端位置，量測可用纜長、垂度和海床接觸，核對可能卡阻。把幾何變化連回經驗證的力位移曲線，另查高水位時岸上構件的垂直反力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot line-end positions at different levels on one datum, measuring available length, sag and seabed contact and checking obstructions. Relate geometric changes to a verified force-displacement curve and separately examine vertical reactions on shore attachments during higher water. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以同一基準畫高低水位的纜端位置，量測可用纜長、垂度和海床接觸，核對可能卡阻。把幾何變化連回經驗證的力位移曲線，另查高水位時岸上構件的垂直反力。","observationEn":"Site practice: Plot line-end positions at different levels on one datum, measuring available length, sag and seabed contact and checking obstructions. Relate geometric changes to a verified force-displacement curve and separately examine vertical reactions on shore attachments during higher water.","failure":"注意干擾：高水位使纜線接近拉直時，剩餘伸長可能轉為很大的張力增量；低水位則可能增加海床磨耗。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: As a line straightens at high water, further extension can produce a large tension increment, while low water increases seabed abrasion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同一基準畫高低水位的纜端位置，量測可用纜長、垂度和海床接觸，核對可能卡阻。把幾何變化連回經驗證的力位移曲線，另查高水位時岸上構件的垂直反力。","textEn":"Plot line-end positions at different levels on one datum, measuring available length, sag and seabed contact and checking obstructions. Relate geometric changes to a verified force-displacement curve and separately examine vertical reactions on shore attachments during higher water.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以同一基準畫高低水位的纜端位置，量測可用纜長、垂度和海床接觸，核對可能卡阻。把幾何變化連回經驗證的力位移曲線，另查高水位時岸上構件的垂直反力。","textEn":"Plot line-end positions at different levels on one datum, measuring available length, sag and seabed contact and checking obstructions. Relate geometric changes to a verified force-displacement curve and separately examine vertical reactions on shore attachments during higher water.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「潮位幾何與鬆弛」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tidal geometry and slack\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。","以同一基準畫高低水位的纜端位置，量測可用纜長、垂度和海床接觸，核對可能卡阻。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface.","Plot line-end positions at different levels on one datum, measuring available length, sag and seabed contact and checking obstructions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以同一基準畫高低水位的纜端位置，量測可用纜長、垂度和海床接觸，核對可能卡阻。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot line-end positions at different levels on one datum, measuring available length, sag and seabed contact and checking obstructions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b291-v15-24","title":"潮位幾何與鬆弛：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tidal geometry and slack: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「潮位幾何與鬆弛」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tidal geometry and slack” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高水位使纜線接近拉直時，剩餘伸長可能轉為很大的張力增量；低水位則可能增加海床磨耗。只檢查中潮幾何，無法涵蓋兩端的不同行為。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"As a line straightens at high water, further extension can produce a large tension increment, while low water increases seabed abrasion. Mid-tide geometry alone cannot cover these different behaviors at the ends of the tidal range. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設水平距10m，高差由1變3m，直線距由√101=10.0499增至√109=10.4403m，增0.3904m；非鏈條張力模型。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Chord length rises10.0499to10.4403m, an increase0.3904m; this is not a catenary-tension model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高水位使纜線接近拉直時，剩餘伸長可能轉為很大的張力增量；低水位則可能增加海床磨耗。只檢查中潮幾何，無法涵蓋兩端的不同行為。","textEn":"As a line straightens at high water, further extension can produce a large tension increment, while low water increases seabed abrasion. Mid-tide geometry alone cannot cover these different behaviors at the ends of the tidal range.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「潮位幾何與鬆弛」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tidal geometry and slack\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["高水位使纜線接近拉直時，剩餘伸長可能轉為很大的張力增量；低水位則可能增加海床磨耗。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。"],"optionsEn":["As a line straightens at high water, further extension can produce a large tension increment, while low water increases seabed abrasion.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高水位使纜線接近拉直時，剩餘伸長可能轉為很大的張力增量；低水位則可能增加海床磨耗。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"As a line straightens at high water, further extension can produce a large tension increment, while low water increases seabed abrasion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b291-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「並聯恢復剛度」與「水平振盪時間尺度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Parallel restoring stiffness\" and \"Horizontal oscillation timescale\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b291-v15-25","title":"並聯恢復剛度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Parallel restoring stiffness: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「並聯恢復剛度」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Parallel restoring stiffness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"多條纜的水平恢復力可以在特定平衡點線性化，但只有同方向、同時受力的小位移增量才直接相加。幾何旋轉與單向受拉特性會改變參與線數，整個系統還有浮台轉動自由度；單一總剛度不代表所有位移方向和幅度都相同。 假設兩個同向並聯線性恢復分量k1=20、k2=30kN/m，受增量力10kN時x=10/(20+30)=0.20m；兩者均持續受力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「並聯恢復剛度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Horizontal restoring force can be linearized about one equilibrium, with direct addition applying only to simultaneously engaged, collinear small-displacement increments. Geometry and tension-only behavior change the active lines, and the dock also rotates. One total stiffness cannot describe every direction and amplitude, so its use must remain tied to the specified equilibrium state and local motion coordinate. Assume two collinear parallel restoring components20and30kN/m remain engaged. An incremental10kN gives x=10/50=0.20m near that equilibrium. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Parallel restoring stiffness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「並聯恢復剛度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Parallel restoring stiffness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-25-k1","title":"並聯恢復剛度","titleEn":"Parallel restoring stiffness","text":"多條纜的水平恢復力可以在特定平衡點線性化，但只有同方向、同時受力的小位移增量才直接相加。幾何旋轉與單向受拉特性會改變參與線數，整個系統還有浮台轉動自由度；單一總剛度不代表所有位移方向和幅度都相同。","textEn":"Horizontal restoring force can be linearized about one equilibrium, with direct addition applying only to simultaneously engaged, collinear small-displacement increments. Geometry and tension-only behavior change the active lines, and the dock also rotates.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「並聯恢復剛度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Parallel restoring stiffness\" is correct?","options":["所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。","多條纜的水平恢復力可以在特定平衡點線性化，但只有同方向、同時受力的小位移增量才直接相加。","自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction.","Horizontal restoring force can be linearized about one equilibrium, with direct addition applying only to simultaneously engaged, collinear small-displacement increments.","A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information."],"answer":1,"explanation":"多條纜的水平恢復力可以在特定平衡點線性化，但只有同方向、同時受力的小位移增量才直接相加。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Horizontal restoring force can be linearized about one equilibrium, with direct addition applying only to simultaneously engaged, collinear small-displacement increments. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b291-v15-26","title":"並聯恢復剛度：定量估算","titleEn":"Parallel restoring stiffness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「並聯恢復剛度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Parallel restoring stiffness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設兩個同向並聯線性恢復分量k1=20、k2=30kN/m，受增量力10kN時x=10/(20+30)=0.20m；兩者均持續受力。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume two collinear parallel restoring components20and30kN/m remain engaged. An incremental10kN gives x=10/50=0.20m near that equilibrium. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將每條纜的力位移投影到相同水平座標，檢查小位移試驗期間是否有鬆弛或滑移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Project each force-displacement response onto the same horizontal coordinate and check slack or sliding during small-motion tests.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設兩個同向並聯線性恢復分量k1=20、k2=30kN/m，受增量力10kN時x=10/(20+30)=0.20m；兩者均持續受力。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume two collinear parallel restoring components20and30kN/m remain engaged. An incremental10kN gives x=10/50=0.20m near that equilibrium.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「並聯恢復剛度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Parallel restoring stiffness\", which statement holds?","options":["理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。","浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading.","Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b291-v15-27","title":"並聯恢復剛度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Parallel restoring stiffness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「並聯恢復剛度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Parallel restoring stiffness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將每條纜的力位移投影到相同水平座標，檢查小位移試驗期間是否有鬆弛或滑移。比較正反向剛度與轉動耦合，記錄適用平衡點，不能將局部斜率延伸到極端偏移。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Project each force-displacement response onto the same horizontal coordinate and check slack or sliding during small-motion tests. Compare opposite directions and rotational coupling, recording the equilibrium point instead of extending one local slope to extreme offsets of the dock. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將每條纜的力位移投影到相同水平座標，檢查小位移試驗期間是否有鬆弛或滑移。比較正反向剛度與轉動耦合，記錄適用平衡點，不能將局部斜率延伸到極端偏移。","observationEn":"Site practice: Project each force-displacement response onto the same horizontal coordinate and check slack or sliding during small-motion tests. Compare opposite directions and rotational coupling, recording the equilibrium point instead of extending one local slope to extreme offsets of the dock.","failure":"注意干擾：一條纜失去預張會讓原先並聯分擔消失，總位移可能突然增加。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Loss of pretension removes a previously active parallel contribution and can sharply increase displacement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將每條纜的力位移投影到相同水平座標，檢查小位移試驗期間是否有鬆弛或滑移。比較正反向剛度與轉動耦合，記錄適用平衡點，不能將局部斜率延伸到極端偏移。","textEn":"Project each force-displacement response onto the same horizontal coordinate and check slack or sliding during small-motion tests. Compare opposite directions and rotational coupling, recording the equilibrium point instead of extending one local slope to extreme offsets of the dock.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將每條纜的力位移投影到相同水平座標，檢查小位移試驗期間是否有鬆弛或滑移。比較正反向剛度與轉動耦合，記錄適用平衡點，不能將局部斜率延伸到極端偏移。","textEn":"Project each force-displacement response onto the same horizontal coordinate and check slack or sliding during small-motion tests. Compare opposite directions and rotational coupling, recording the equilibrium point instead of extending one local slope to extreme offsets of the dock.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「並聯恢復剛度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Parallel restoring stiffness\"?","options":["將每條纜的力位移投影到相同水平座標，檢查小位移試驗期間是否有鬆弛或滑移。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。"],"optionsEn":["Project each force-displacement response onto the same horizontal coordinate and check slack or sliding during small-motion tests.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將每條纜的力位移投影到相同水平座標，檢查小位移試驗期間是否有鬆弛或滑移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Project each force-displacement response onto the same horizontal coordinate and check slack or sliding during small-motion tests. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b291-v15-28","title":"並聯恢復剛度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Parallel restoring stiffness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「並聯恢復剛度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Parallel restoring stiffness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"一條纜失去預張會讓原先並聯分擔消失，總位移可能突然增加。若只用所有材料EA相加而未投影幾何，會高估真正提供的水平恢復剛度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Loss of pretension removes a previously active parallel contribution and can sharply increase displacement. Adding material EA values without geometric projection also overstates the horizontal restoring stiffness actually available to the floating structure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設兩個同向並聯線性恢復分量k1=20、k2=30kN/m，受增量力10kN時x=10/(20+30)=0.20m；兩者均持續受力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: An incremental10kN gives x=10/50=0.20m near that equilibrium.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"一條纜失去預張會讓原先並聯分擔消失，總位移可能突然增加。若只用所有材料EA相加而未投影幾何，會高估真正提供的水平恢復剛度。","textEn":"Loss of pretension removes a previously active parallel contribution and can sharply increase displacement. Adding material EA values without geometric projection also overstates the horizontal restoring stiffness actually available to the floating structure.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「並聯恢復剛度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Parallel restoring stiffness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","一條纜失去預張會讓原先並聯分擔消失，總位移可能突然增加。","自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Loss of pretension removes a previously active parallel contribution and can sharply increase displacement.","A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information."],"answer":1,"explanation":"一條纜失去預張會讓原先並聯分擔消失，總位移可能突然增加。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Loss of pretension removes a previously active parallel contribution and can sharply increase displacement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b291-v15-29","title":"水平振盪時間尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Horizontal oscillation timescale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「水平振盪時間尺度」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Horizontal oscillation timescale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"浮碼頭質量、附加水質量與恢復剛度共同決定自然振盪尺度，與波浪或船行波頻率接近時反應可能放大。單自由度無阻尼模型只能估計週期，不能預測峰值或共振幅度；實際纜繩非線性、摩擦及輻射阻尼必須另行識別並與觀測對照。 假設已含附加質量的有效m=100000kg、水平k=50000N/m，Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s；無阻尼線性示意。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水平振盪時間尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Dock mass, hydrodynamic added mass and restoring stiffness set a natural timescale, with possible amplification near wave or wake frequencies. An undamped single-degree model estimates period only, not peak response or resonance amplitude. Real line nonlinearity, friction and radiation damping require separate identification and observation before the simplified timing relation can support interpretation of actual motion. Assume effective mass100000kg already includes added mass and horizontal stiffness50000N/m. Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s for an undamped linear illustration. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Horizontal oscillation timescale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水平振盪時間尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Horizontal oscillation timescale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-29-k1","title":"水平振盪時間尺度","titleEn":"Horizontal oscillation timescale","text":"浮碼頭質量、附加水質量與恢復剛度共同決定自然振盪尺度，與波浪或船行波頻率接近時反應可能放大。單自由度無阻尼模型只能估計週期，不能預測峰值或共振幅度；實際纜繩非線性、摩擦及輻射阻尼必須另行識別並與觀測對照。","textEn":"Dock mass, hydrodynamic added mass and restoring stiffness set a natural timescale, with possible amplification near wave or wake frequencies. An undamped single-degree model estimates period only, not peak response or resonance amplitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水平振盪時間尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Horizontal oscillation timescale\" is correct?","options":["自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。","引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。","浮碼頭質量、附加水質量與恢復剛度共同決定自然振盪尺度，與波浪或船行波頻率接近時反應可能放大。"],"optionsEn":["A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information.","Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements.","Dock mass, hydrodynamic added mass and restoring stiffness set a natural timescale, with possible amplification near wave or wake frequencies."],"answer":2,"explanation":"浮碼頭質量、附加水質量與恢復剛度共同決定自然振盪尺度，與波浪或船行波頻率接近時反應可能放大。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Dock mass, hydrodynamic added mass and restoring stiffness set a natural timescale, with possible amplification near wave or wake frequencies. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b291-v15-30","title":"水平振盪時間尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Horizontal oscillation timescale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水平振盪時間尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Horizontal oscillation timescale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設已含附加質量的有效m=100000kg、水平k=50000N/m，Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s；無阻尼線性示意。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume effective mass100000kg already includes added mass and horizontal stiffness50000N/m. Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s for an undamped linear illustration. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從小幅自由衰減或環境振動記錄辨識週期，核對質量、纜態與潮位是否與模型一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Identify period from small-amplitude decay or ambient motion with matching mass, line state and tide.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設已含附加質量的有效m=100000kg、水平k=50000N/m，Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s；無阻尼線性示意。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume effective mass100000kg already includes added mass and horizontal stiffness50000N/m. Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s for an undamped linear illustration.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水平振盪時間尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Horizontal oscillation timescale\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。","遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves.","A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b291-v15-31","title":"水平振盪時間尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Horizontal oscillation timescale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水平振盪時間尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Horizontal oscillation timescale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從小幅自由衰減或環境振動記錄辨識週期，核對質量、纜態與潮位是否與模型一致。比較外力頻譜並另估阻尼，保留大位移時非線性特徵，不用單一週期推定峰值張力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Identify period from small-amplitude decay or ambient motion with matching mass, line state and tide. Compare forcing spectra and estimate damping separately, retaining nonlinear behavior at larger offsets rather than using one period to infer maximum line tension. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：從小幅自由衰減或環境振動記錄辨識週期，核對質量、纜態與潮位是否與模型一致。比較外力頻譜並另估阻尼，保留大位移時非線性特徵，不用單一週期推定峰值張力。","observationEn":"Site practice: Identify period from small-amplitude decay or ambient motion with matching mass, line state and tide. Compare forcing spectra and estimate damping separately, retaining nonlinear behavior at larger offsets rather than using one period to infer maximum line tension.","failure":"注意干擾：附加質量重複計入會拉長預測週期，纜剛度隨潮位改變則移動共振區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Double-counted added mass lengthens the predicted period, while tide-dependent line stiffness shifts the resonance range. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從小幅自由衰減或環境振動記錄辨識週期，核對質量、纜態與潮位是否與模型一致。比較外力頻譜並另估阻尼，保留大位移時非線性特徵，不用單一週期推定峰值張力。","textEn":"Identify period from small-amplitude decay or ambient motion with matching mass, line state and tide. Compare forcing spectra and estimate damping separately, retaining nonlinear behavior at larger offsets rather than using one period to infer maximum line tension.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"從小幅自由衰減或環境振動記錄辨識週期，核對質量、纜態與潮位是否與模型一致。比較外力頻譜並另估阻尼，保留大位移時非線性特徵，不用單一週期推定峰值張力。","textEn":"Identify period from small-amplitude decay or ambient motion with matching mass, line state and tide. Compare forcing spectra and estimate damping separately, retaining nonlinear behavior at larger offsets rather than using one period to infer maximum line tension.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水平振盪時間尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Horizontal oscillation timescale\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","從小幅自由衰減或環境振動記錄辨識週期，核對質量、纜態與潮位是否與模型一致。","所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Identify period from small-amplitude decay or ambient motion with matching mass, line state and tide.","Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"從小幅自由衰減或環境振動記錄辨識週期，核對質量、纜態與潮位是否與模型一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Identify period from small-amplitude decay or ambient motion with matching mass, line state and tide. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b291-v15-32","title":"水平振盪時間尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Horizontal oscillation timescale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水平振盪時間尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Horizontal oscillation timescale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"附加質量重複計入會拉長預測週期，纜剛度隨潮位改變則移動共振區。即使週期吻合，錯誤阻尼仍可能讓預測振幅與實測相差很大。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Double-counted added mass lengthens the predicted period, while tide-dependent line stiffness shifts the resonance range. Matching period alone does not establish correct amplitude because an incorrect damping estimate can still produce a large response discrepancy. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設已含附加質量的有效m=100000kg、水平k=50000N/m，Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s；無阻尼線性示意。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s for an undamped linear illustration.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"附加質量重複計入會拉長預測週期，纜剛度隨潮位改變則移動共振區。即使週期吻合，錯誤阻尼仍可能讓預測振幅與實測相差很大。","textEn":"Double-counted added mass lengthens the predicted period, while tide-dependent line stiffness shifts the resonance range. Matching period alone does not establish correct amplitude because an incorrect damping estimate can still produce a large response discrepancy.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水平振盪時間尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Horizontal oscillation timescale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。","附加質量重複計入會拉長預測週期，纜剛度隨潮位改變則移動共振區。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements.","Double-counted added mass lengthens the predicted period, while tide-dependent line stiffness shifts the resonance range."],"answer":2,"explanation":"附加質量重複計入會拉長預測週期，纜剛度隨潮位改變則移動共振區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Double-counted added mass lengthens the predicted period, while tide-dependent line stiffness shifts the resonance range. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b291-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「引橋坡度與行程」與「浮力儲備與損艙」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Gangway slope and travel\" and \"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b291-v15-33","title":"引橋坡度與行程：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Gangway slope and travel: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「引橋坡度與行程」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gangway slope and travel” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"岸上平台固定而浮台升降，引橋坡度及端部滑移隨水位變化，與纜繩容許位移需要共同檢查。幾何斜率不是無障礙或使用合格證明，轉折、扶手、表面及動態運動亦有要求；在水平長度和實際橋長之間混用會導致角度與行程錯誤。 假設高差1.2m、水平投影12m，坡度10%、角度atan(1.2/12)=5.711°，斜長12.0599m；不是通行允收值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「引橋坡度與行程」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A fixed shore platform and moving pontoon change gangway slope and end travel, which must be compatible with mooring offsets. Geometric grade is not proof of accessibility or acceptable use; transitions, rails, surfaces and dynamic movement matter too. Confusing horizontal run with actual span length corrupts angle and travel calculations even when the height difference is measured correctly. Assume rise1.2m and horizontal run12m. Grade is10%,angle5.711° and sloping length12.0599m, not an access acceptance criterion. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gangway slope and travel” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「引橋坡度與行程」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gangway slope and travel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-33-k1","title":"引橋坡度與行程","titleEn":"Gangway slope and travel","text":"岸上平台固定而浮台升降，引橋坡度及端部滑移隨水位變化，與纜繩容許位移需要共同檢查。幾何斜率不是無障礙或使用合格證明，轉折、扶手、表面及動態運動亦有要求；在水平長度和實際橋長之間混用會導致角度與行程錯誤。","textEn":"A fixed shore platform and moving pontoon change gangway slope and end travel, which must be compatible with mooring offsets. Geometric grade is not proof of accessibility or acceptable use; transitions, rails, surfaces and dynamic movement matter too.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「引橋坡度與行程」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gangway slope and travel\" is correct?","options":["岸上平台固定而浮台升降，引橋坡度及端部滑移隨水位變化，與纜繩容許位移需要共同檢查。","引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。","理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。"],"optionsEn":["A fixed shore platform and moving pontoon change gangway slope and end travel, which must be compatible with mooring offsets.","Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements.","All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading."],"answer":0,"explanation":"岸上平台固定而浮台升降，引橋坡度及端部滑移隨水位變化，與纜繩容許位移需要共同檢查。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A fixed shore platform and moving pontoon change gangway slope and end travel, which must be compatible with mooring offsets. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b291-v15-34","title":"引橋坡度與行程：定量估算","titleEn":"Gangway slope and travel: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「引橋坡度與行程」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gangway slope and travel” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設高差1.2m、水平投影12m，坡度10%、角度atan(1.2/12)=5.711°，斜長12.0599m；不是通行允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume rise1.2m and horizontal run12m. Grade is10%,angle5.711° and sloping length12.0599m, not an access acceptance criterion. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分別標示水平投影、實際橋長及端部可滑行範圍，在高低潮與浮台偏移組合下重畫幾何。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Distinguish horizontal run, span length and available end travel, redrawing geometry for combined tide and dock offsets.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設高差1.2m、水平投影12m，坡度10%、角度atan(1.2/12)=5.711°，斜長12.0599m；不是通行允收值。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume rise1.2m and horizontal run12m. Grade is10%,angle5.711° and sloping length12.0599m, not an access acceptance criterion.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「引橋坡度與行程」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gangway slope and travel\", which statement holds?","options":["浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。"],"optionsEn":["Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b291-v15-35","title":"引橋坡度與行程：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gangway slope and travel: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「引橋坡度與行程」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gangway slope and travel” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分別標示水平投影、實際橋長及端部可滑行範圍，在高低潮與浮台偏移組合下重畫幾何。依適用無障礙及設施設計要求檢查全路徑，另記防滑、夾點與動態運動的驗證證據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Distinguish horizontal run, span length and available end travel, redrawing geometry for combined tide and dock offsets. Check the entire route against applicable accessibility and facility requirements, retaining evidence for slip resistance, pinch interfaces and dynamic movement separately. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分別標示水平投影、實際橋長及端部可滑行範圍，在高低潮與浮台偏移組合下重畫幾何。依適用無障礙及設施設計要求檢查全路徑，另記防滑、夾點與動態運動的驗證證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Distinguish horizontal run, span length and available end travel, redrawing geometry for combined tide and dock offsets. Check the entire route against applicable accessibility and facility requirements, retaining evidence for slip resistance, pinch interfaces and dynamic movement separately.","failure":"注意干擾：只看平均坡度會漏掉端部短折角，浮台水平偏移也可能耗盡滑座行程。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Average grade can hide a short end transition, and horizontal pontoon movement can exhaust sliding travel. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分別標示水平投影、實際橋長及端部可滑行範圍，在高低潮與浮台偏移組合下重畫幾何。依適用無障礙及設施設計要求檢查全路徑，另記防滑、夾點與動態運動的驗證證據。","textEn":"Distinguish horizontal run, span length and available end travel, redrawing geometry for combined tide and dock offsets. Check the entire route against applicable accessibility and facility requirements, retaining evidence for slip resistance, pinch interfaces and dynamic movement separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分別標示水平投影、實際橋長及端部可滑行範圍，在高低潮與浮台偏移組合下重畫幾何。依適用無障礙及設施設計要求檢查全路徑，另記防滑、夾點與動態運動的驗證證據。","textEn":"Distinguish horizontal run, span length and available end travel, redrawing geometry for combined tide and dock offsets. Check the entire route against applicable accessibility and facility requirements, retaining evidence for slip resistance, pinch interfaces and dynamic movement separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「引橋坡度與行程」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gangway slope and travel\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。","分別標示水平投影、實際橋長及端部可滑行範圍，在高低潮與浮台偏移組合下重畫幾何。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.","Distinguish horizontal run, span length and available end travel, redrawing geometry for combined tide and dock offsets."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分別標示水平投影、實際橋長及端部可滑行範圍，在高低潮與浮台偏移組合下重畫幾何。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Distinguish horizontal run, span length and available end travel, redrawing geometry for combined tide and dock offsets. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b291-v15-36","title":"引橋坡度與行程：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gangway slope and travel: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「引橋坡度與行程」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gangway slope and travel” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看平均坡度會漏掉端部短折角，浮台水平偏移也可能耗盡滑座行程。即使靜態幾何仍可通行，波動造成的相對運動仍需在使用情境中評估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Average grade can hide a short end transition, and horizontal pontoon movement can exhaust sliding travel. Even apparently passable static geometry requires assessment of relative wave-induced movement within the actual use context of the facility. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設高差1.2m、水平投影12m，坡度10%、角度atan(1.2/12)=5.711°，斜長12.0599m；不是通行允收值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Grade is10%,angle5.711° and sloping length12.0599m, not an access acceptance criterion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看平均坡度會漏掉端部短折角，浮台水平偏移也可能耗盡滑座行程。即使靜態幾何仍可通行，波動造成的相對運動仍需在使用情境中評估。","textEn":"Average grade can hide a short end transition, and horizontal pontoon movement can exhaust sliding travel. Even apparently passable static geometry requires assessment of relative wave-induced movement within the actual use context of the facility.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「引橋坡度與行程」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gangway slope and travel\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只看平均坡度會漏掉端部短折角，浮台水平偏移也可能耗盡滑座行程。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。"],"optionsEn":["Average grade can hide a short end transition, and horizontal pontoon movement can exhaust sliding travel.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只看平均坡度會漏掉端部短折角，浮台水平偏移也可能耗盡滑座行程。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Average grade can hide a short end transition, and horizontal pontoon movement can exhaust sliding travel. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b291-v15-37","title":"浮力儲備與損艙：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「浮力儲備與損艙」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Buoyant reserve and compartment loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"浮筒損壞會改變可用排水體積及重量分布，分艙的目的之一是限制局部進水影響。完整密閉體的總容積不是損壞後可用浮力，且浸沒到頂的理論餘量不含動態乾舷需求；應分開完整和損艙狀態，追蹤何處先失去通達或穩定功能。 假設密閉可排水體積120m³、海水1025kg/m³、總質量100000kg，至全浸沒理論質量餘量23000kg；不是允許載重。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「浮力儲備與損艙」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Damage changes available buoyant volume and weight distribution, while compartments limit the extent of flooding. Total enclosed volume in the intact state is not available buoyancy after damage, and a theoretical reserve to deck immersion excludes dynamic freeboard needs. Intact and damaged states need separate treatment, identifying where access or stability is lost before relying on a total reserve number. Assume sealed displacement capacity120m³,seawater1025kg/m³ and mass100000kg. Theoretical reserve to full immersion is23000kg, not an allowable additional load. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Buoyant reserve and compartment loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「浮力儲備與損艙」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Buoyant reserve and compartment loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-37-k1","title":"浮力儲備與損艙","titleEn":"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss","text":"浮筒損壞會改變可用排水體積及重量分布，分艙的目的之一是限制局部進水影響。完整密閉體的總容積不是損壞後可用浮力，且浸沒到頂的理論餘量不含動態乾舷需求；應分開完整和損艙狀態，追蹤何處先失去通達或穩定功能。","textEn":"Damage changes available buoyant volume and weight distribution, while compartments limit the extent of flooding. Total enclosed volume in the intact state is not available buoyancy after damage, and a theoretical reserve to deck immersion excludes dynamic freeboard needs.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「浮力儲備與損艙」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss\" is correct?","options":["理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。","浮筒損壞會改變可用排水體積及重量分布，分艙的目的之一是限制局部進水影響。","只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。"],"optionsEn":["All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading.","Damage changes available buoyant volume and weight distribution, while compartments limit the extent of flooding.","Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves."],"answer":1,"explanation":"浮筒損壞會改變可用排水體積及重量分布，分艙的目的之一是限制局部進水影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Damage changes available buoyant volume and weight distribution, while compartments limit the extent of flooding. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b291-v15-38","title":"浮力儲備與損艙：定量估算","titleEn":"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「浮力儲備與損艙」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Buoyant reserve and compartment loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設密閉可排水體積120m³、海水1025kg/m³、總質量100000kg，至全浸沒理論質量餘量23000kg；不是允許載重。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume sealed displacement capacity120m³,seawater1025kg/m³ and mass100000kg. Theoretical reserve to full immersion is23000kg, not an allowable additional load. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立分艙體積和重量位置清單，核對水密檢查及進水警示，分別畫完整與指定損艙吃水姿態。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Inventory compartment volumes and weight locations, checking watertightness and flooding detection.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設密閉可排水體積120m³、海水1025kg/m³、總質量100000kg，至全浸沒理論質量餘量23000kg；不是允許載重。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume sealed displacement capacity120m³,seawater1025kg/m³ and mass100000kg. Theoretical reserve to full immersion is23000kg, not an allowable additional load.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「浮力儲備與損艙」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss\", which statement holds?","options":["遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。","所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface.","Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b291-v15-39","title":"浮力儲備與損艙：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「浮力儲備與損艙」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Buoyant reserve and compartment loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立分艙體積和重量位置清單，核對水密檢查及進水警示，分別畫完整與指定損艙吃水姿態。將理論浮力餘量與最低乾舷、穩性及使用條件分開，不讓總容積掩蓋局部進水。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Inventory compartment volumes and weight locations, checking watertightness and flooding detection. Draw intact and specified damaged attitudes separately and distinguish theoretical buoyant reserve from freeboard, stability and use requirements so total volume does not hide localized flooding. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立分艙體積和重量位置清單，核對水密檢查及進水警示，分別畫完整與指定損艙吃水姿態。將理論浮力餘量與最低乾舷、穩性及使用條件分開，不讓總容積掩蓋局部進水。","observationEn":"Site practice: Inventory compartment volumes and weight locations, checking watertightness and flooding detection. Draw intact and specified damaged attitudes separately and distinguish theoretical buoyant reserve from freeboard, stability and use requirements so total volume does not hide localized flooding.","failure":"注意干擾：某一端進水可能先造成傾斜和引橋不對位，總剩餘浮力尚大也不表示功能完整。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Flooding at one end can first cause heel and gangway misalignment even with substantial remaining total buoyancy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立分艙體積和重量位置清單，核對水密檢查及進水警示，分別畫完整與指定損艙吃水姿態。將理論浮力餘量與最低乾舷、穩性及使用條件分開，不讓總容積掩蓋局部進水。","textEn":"Inventory compartment volumes and weight locations, checking watertightness and flooding detection. Draw intact and specified damaged attitudes separately and distinguish theoretical buoyant reserve from freeboard, stability and use requirements so total volume does not hide localized flooding.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立分艙體積和重量位置清單，核對水密檢查及進水警示，分別畫完整與指定損艙吃水姿態。將理論浮力餘量與最低乾舷、穩性及使用條件分開，不讓總容積掩蓋局部進水。","textEn":"Inventory compartment volumes and weight locations, checking watertightness and flooding detection. Draw intact and specified damaged attitudes separately and distinguish theoretical buoyant reserve from freeboard, stability and use requirements so total volume does not hide localized flooding.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「浮力儲備與損艙」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss\"?","options":["建立分艙體積和重量位置清單，核對水密檢查及進水警示，分別畫完整與指定損艙吃水姿態。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。"],"optionsEn":["Inventory compartment volumes and weight locations, checking watertightness and flooding detection.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"建立分艙體積和重量位置清單，核對水密檢查及進水警示，分別畫完整與指定損艙吃水姿態。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Inventory compartment volumes and weight locations, checking watertightness and flooding detection. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b291-v15-40","title":"浮力儲備與損艙：失效診斷","titleEn":"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「浮力儲備與損艙」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Buoyant reserve and compartment loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"某一端進水可能先造成傾斜和引橋不對位，總剩餘浮力尚大也不表示功能完整。把全浸沒餘量當可加載量，會忽略波浪、進水和人員偏載所需的空間。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Flooding at one end can first cause heel and gangway misalignment even with substantial remaining total buoyancy. Treating reserve to full immersion as permissible loading ignores the space needed for waves, flooding and eccentric occupancy. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設密閉可排水體積120m³、海水1025kg/m³、總質量100000kg，至全浸沒理論質量餘量23000kg；不是允許載重。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Theoretical reserve to full immersion is23000kg, not an allowable additional load.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"某一端進水可能先造成傾斜和引橋不對位，總剩餘浮力尚大也不表示功能完整。把全浸沒餘量當可加載量，會忽略波浪、進水和人員偏載所需的空間。","textEn":"Flooding at one end can first cause heel and gangway misalignment even with substantial remaining total buoyancy. Treating reserve to full immersion as permissible loading ignores the space needed for waves, flooding and eccentric occupancy.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「浮力儲備與損艙」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","某一端進水可能先造成傾斜和引橋不對位，總剩餘浮力尚大也不表示功能完整。","只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Flooding at one end can first cause heel and gangway misalignment even with substantial remaining total buoyancy.","Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves."],"answer":1,"explanation":"某一端進水可能先造成傾斜和引橋不對位，總剩餘浮力尚大也不表示功能完整。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Flooding at one end can first cause heel and gangway misalignment even with substantial remaining total buoyancy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
